# frontend/ - Excelsior React SPA (v2)

Greenfield React 19 + Vite 6 + TypeScript single-page app that replaces the
legacy vanilla-JS site under `public/`. This is the production frontend going
forward.

## Visual source of truth
- Design decisions live in repo-root `STYLE_GUIDE_V2.md`. Update it whenever you
  change visual patterns, tokens, or add a screen.
- Architecture/reference: `docs/current/FRONTEND_V2.md`.
- Draw Hand + Simulate KO: `docs/current/DRAW_HAND_FEATURE.md`, `docs/current/SIMULATE_KO_FEATURE.md`.

## Structure
- `src/app/` - router, AuthProvider, ProtectedRoute (cross-cutting app wiring).
- `src/components/` - reusable presentational/UI components. Each component dir
  has `Component.tsx`, `Component.css`, `Component.md` (context), `index.ts`.
- `src/features/` - route-level pages (login, home, database, collection,
  deck-selection, deck-editor). Pages compose shared components.
- `src/lib/` - non-UI logic: `api/` (typed fetch wrappers), `images/`,
  `catalog/`, `collection/`, `layout/`, `decks/` (draw hand, KO, catalog index).
- `src/styles/` - `tokens.css` (design tokens) + `global.css` (reset + base).
- Home "Recent Updates" cards load from `GET /api/v1/recent-updates` (`lib/api/recent-updates.ts`).

## Conventions
- Server state via TanStack Query; cross-cutting state via `useAuth()` /
  `useLayoutMode()` hooks.
- All data calls go to `/api/v1/*`; session auth uses legacy `/api/auth/*`.
  Always send credentials (cookies) via the shared api client.
- Card images: never hardcode paths. Use the `CardImage` component / the
  `cardImages.ts` helpers, which apply the CDN base and thumbnail rules.
- Mobile vs desktop: never branch on user-agent. Use `useLayoutMode()` (900px
  breakpoint, `preferDesktopLayout` override) and `.layout-mobile` /
  `.layout-desktop` scoped CSS.

## Dev
- **Open the app at `http://localhost:5173`** (not :8085). Requires root
  `npm run dev` running in parallel for the API backend on :8085.
- `npm run dev` (Vite :5173) proxies `/api`, `/health`, `/src/resources`, `/js`
  to the Express backend on :8085.
- `npm run build` outputs to `dist/`, served in prod by Express
  `src/routes/spaIndexPath.ts`.

## Guest rules (product)
- GUEST users: `+ Deck` is disabled on the Database view; guest collection is
  stored only in `localStorage`. Do not re-enable guest DB-deck adds without a
  product decision (see docs/current/GUEST_DECK_LESSONS_LEARNED.md).
